{\pard\ql\fs20 Notes: This table reports the variance decomposition of the city-level CPU index obtained from xtsum. The data is collapsed to city-year means. Within-city variance share = within-city variance / total variance. The within-city SD exceeds the between-city SD, confirming that CPU exhibits substantial time variation within cities, providing the identifying variation for our shift-share instrument after county fixed effects absorb cross-sectional differences. The CPU index is sourced from Ma et al. (2023).\par}
